{"title":"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The vertices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11ec7d39f29ddcb2df0f1d1dc83ad21031e4607.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (0,0)\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/caed5b4ff8fe4de9650dc4baded8d3a6c65f5f2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (0,420)\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b95ec39faf944fbc0e2d73a89e1a6478272d58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (560,0)\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />.  The six faces of a die are labeled with two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/e/72eb1fe97f5961e315048f86acfdad20707ea9e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\,$\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" />'s, two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82a2c160f4d201115e2129a78e58d9733be6706d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B\\,$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />'s, and two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/181fc7e4fc45bb8783db936cb7e663284b47b062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C\\,$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />'s.  Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c83199611f1c41b141bc5867a20f6b410f959c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 = (k,m)\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> is chosen in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, and points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08f7bf13148eb00e2d40ef6082f3f8b72eea898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74a2486a7ff5ad2b70c37246c006469af35d6e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_3\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f621098a7200187a4333ac441baed73ca07ec1bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_4, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> are generated by rolling the die repeatedly and applying the rule: If the die shows label <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac38351e9b42d7bd80b3f35d11136ea9b8783dc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d85f327335e6472d45ac13b4b6f7f2742c43af4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L \\in \\{A, B, C\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/668825d6a66db631d7d22d5987c3c5b12b66efcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is the most recently obtained point, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a40e7b62b004655cdd433dc4d23b84e38b93861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{n + 1}^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69eed9a84de94a8b83a1f7db1651c0c804768af3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{P_n L}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />.  Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a17698bcefed02213b8bc2ba14e9b640aab2fff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_7 = (14,92)\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />, what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/16638d3c83e10d580e009bd49a482f0bfd7a58ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + m\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If we have points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b7a40ab0d8178e83fe1b91c511d04b1246059b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdfbe2b8882f9559dc575237eb1cd460933d987c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> and we want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7cc0aaa3c34fd4a50a506fb22de40dfff3ed09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u,v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdfbe2b8882f9559dc575237eb1cd460933d987c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7cc0aaa3c34fd4a50a506fb22de40dfff3ed09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u,v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b7a40ab0d8178e83fe1b91c511d04b1246059b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e835d129d2702a5076d22790be719cdcd194afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=2r-p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d15d341f2bae3989a1d4422473d44787e0dd6ab8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v=2s-q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />. So we start with the point they gave us and work backwards. We make sure all the coordinates stay within the triangle. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/291491f6d4e4f7f8a310a3f71d2bad41289ba297.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P_{n-1}=(x_{n-1},y_{n-1}) = (2x_n\\bmod{560},\\ 2y_n\\bmod{420})\\]\" width=\"405\" height=\"18\" />\nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbc63893db1ca5bf00af0abbf1c44113d8b43dc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_7=(14,92)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a308b7f1019c6a29310d76850db8f6620bcc3fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_7=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93afba35766e0ba9647e45bc16f8ccff3e23475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_7=92$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/b/81bb0ede699cdea9e7b67a44ff3dee8453584fcd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c||ccccccc} n &amp; 7 &amp; 6 &amp; 5 &amp; 4 &amp; 3 &amp; 2 &amp; 1 \\\\ \\hline\\hline x_n &amp; 14 &amp; 28 &amp; 56 &amp; 112 &amp; 224 &amp; 448 &amp; 336 \\\\ \\hline y_n &amp; 92 &amp; 184 &amp; 368 &amp; 316 &amp; 212 &amp; 4 &amp; 8  \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"337\" height=\"64\" />\n</p><p>So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acb34d0444df1e46dd4c0df333cb6cca8abf23e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{344}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f22b669e4803ae525cf8120ca251e2eab025872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa62a365c27d4f2c298262b3e8c7c224550c20a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{th}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> roll that directly influences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfe73ec2e3baebb598f22be04312784ea849d9e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{n + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/e/bee61aa4f75a3aa40fd7ecce03b1aa82a995177d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_7 = \\cfrac{\\cfrac{\\cfrac{P_1 + L_1}2 + L_2}2 + \\cdots}{2\\ldots} = \\frac {(k,m)}{64} + \\frac {L_1}{64} + \\frac {L_2}{32} + \\frac {L_3}{16} + \\frac {L_4}8 + \\frac {L_5}4 + \\frac {L_6}2 = (14,92)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"629\" height=\"77\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nThen quickly checking each addend from the right to the left, we have the following information (remembering that if a point must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, we can just ignore it!): \n</p><p>for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/5/3d519e4151b23b722a656bfc49454b0f833d5c96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {L_6}2,\\frac {L_5}4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"54\" height=\"38\" />, since all addends are nonnegative, a non-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> value will result in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> value greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/403d424cf0f48517174037a871a71d9c35f1796e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$92$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, and we can ignore them,\n</p><p>for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/b/69bfc772d9c84f21768a25822072f7f1ac450883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {L_4}8,\\frac {L_3}{16},\\frac {L_2}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" /> in a similar way, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b93c64526cb8a50e043488218e7eb1c9af4be7d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,420)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> are the only possibilities, \n</p><p>and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f59deca26fc9467a43f0fc395d0560876026ed30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {L_1}{64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"38\" />, all three work. \n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Also, to be in the triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47eb74740bf0bc58faa1404b7f709207e02dc3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le k\\le560$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/99365f73386db7d4a15f796a4d7bb3bcfa07f684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le m\\le420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f22b669e4803ae525cf8120ca251e2eab025872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> is the only point that can possibly influence the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> coordinate other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, we look at that first.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c1617d10ded638012090c384088ab6d797a27c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_1 = (0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/d/31d8c4587d82b6bc45560130067173f8e7e78bdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 2^6\\cdot14 = 64\\cdot14 &gt; 40\\cdot14 = 560$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"283\" height=\"18\" />, \n</p><p>so it can only be that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61fdeee7e2937881087a75ba58b3dbabadde14da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_1 = (560,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f77d51e7c708b6188d8e192d2a78f4d9b6da1ce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 560 = 2^6\\cdot14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a68a22c49be9245bb232edd928d9171541d3b96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies k = 64\\cdot14 - 40\\cdot14 = 24\\cdot14 = 6\\cdot56 = 336$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"389\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNow, considering the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> coordinate, note that if any of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b0231ccdb4fa386b18f5b7a3de4613eb50ee4724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_2,L_3,L_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e13a902eb6a24cf493a2732badd0d151fb4f7672.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> would influence the least, so we test that), \n</p><p>then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf5337af94e7869a6051dd21d735edf91a4b4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {L_2}{32} + \\frac {L_3}{16} + \\frac {L_4}8 &lt; \\frac {420}{16} + \\frac {420}8 = 79\\pm\\epsilon &lt; 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"338\" height=\"38\" />, \n</p><p>which would mean that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/98703619131831353e4a33f4ac5e1ab6c36d0e49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 &gt; 2^6\\cdot(92 - 80) = 64\\cdot12 &gt; 42\\cdot10 = 420\\ge m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"384\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12bc3cfc1f2373c22620a7591632a58a24e40481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_2,L_3,L_4 = (0,420)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, \n</p><p>and now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/f/47f33157913e969158ee6c8e6886aa0938516261.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {P_1}{64} + \\frac {420}{2^5} + \\frac {420}{2^4} + \\frac {420}{2^3} = 92$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"225\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cdb515b47287f1dc3555f46db33a825506cda8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd4167c540d62ba280bd72639926d156ace006f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 64\\cdot92 - 420(2 + 4 + 8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"202\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5d0f80de18d6eed45934d31a87d9b479220b1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 64\\cdot92 - 420\\cdot14= 64(100 - 8) - 14^2\\cdot30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"343\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e861a3c819faf1d43461c2044d32c1b16b21f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 6400 - 512 - (200 - 4)\\cdot30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"230\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328e8f62f98a0f6b06b25d358f496cfeeea22e33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 6400 - 512 - 6000 + 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"212\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f103578dda22cc4bd8cc51327ec862494feb8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= - 112 + 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f26722d27c51da5fe985e0420525ef4bfee4efa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 8$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, \n</p><p>and finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fc258a28b122bcbb671baee0a8f13263a5b7ac4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + m = 336 + 8 = \\boxed{344}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"194\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME\" title=\"1993 AIME\">1993 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1993 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1993\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/